// Fixture: diamond-inheritance base WITH its own variable -- pins the
// finding that FluffOS does NOT deduplicate diamond-inherited variables:
// a base reachable via two separate inherit paths contributes its
// variable block TWICE (once per path), with no virtual-inheritance
// merging. That duplication is caught by the pre-existing
// num_variables_total equality check, independent of the function-table
// comparison.
int dvar;
string fdvx() { return "dvx"; }
mixed try_bind() { mixed fp; return catch(fp = (: fdvx :)); }
